---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import V from '../components/V.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy notice | Route 66 Driving School" description="How Route 66 Driving School uses your personal information.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p>Last updated: 3 October 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {business.name} is run by <V v={business.owner} />, a {business.legalForm}, who is the data controller for the
        information described here. Address: <V v={business.address} />. Email:
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}><V v={business.email} /></a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>When you contact us</strong> by WhatsApp, phone or email: your name, phone number and anything you
          tell us, such as your area and availability. We use this to reply and arrange lessons. Lawful basis: taking
          steps at your request before a contract.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>When you book lessons</strong>: your pick-up address, provisional licence details, lesson and test
          dates, and payment records. Lawful bases: contract (to give you lessons), legal obligation (tax records) and
          legitimate interests (insurance).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website visits</strong>: our web host, Cloudflare, processes visitor IP addresses in server logs to
          keep the site secure. Lawful basis: legitimate interests.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>WhatsApp</h2>
      <p>
        Our WhatsApp buttons are plain links. Nothing from WhatsApp loads on this website. If you message us, WhatsApp
        (Meta) processes your messages under its own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>This website does not set cookies.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We don't sell your information. We use a small number of service providers: Cloudflare (website hosting and
        email forwarding) and WhatsApp (Meta) if you message us there. We may share details with DVSA when booking or
        managing driving tests, or where the law requires it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some of these providers may process data outside the UK. Where they do, they use UK-approved safeguards such as
        the UK International Data Transfer Addendum or the UK–US data bridge.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not lead to lessons are deleted within 12 months. Pupil records are kept for up to 6 years
        after your last lesson for accounting and insurance purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete your information, restrict or object to how we use it, or ask for a copy to
        take elsewhere. Contact us using the details above and we'll reply within one month. If you're unhappy with how
        we handle your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
